  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge will build over the plains this weekend\nallowing highs to warm into the upper 80s to the middle 90s\nSaturday and Sunday. \n\nThe region will be in an upper level northwest flow pattern this\nweekend with the ridge to the east of the area. The models are\nshowing an upper level disturbance moving through the northwest\nflow Friday night into Saturday morning and again Saturday \nnight into Sunday morning. Showers and thunderstorms will be \npossible ahead of the disturbance. There are still questions on \nthe track of the disturbance and convection and what portions of\nthe area will be impacted. Locally heavy rainfall will be \npossible if a complex of showers and storms can develop and move\nthrough the area. \n\nThe ensemble model members show and upper level trough and cold\nfront moving out of the plains by the middle of next week.\nHowever, the models differ on the track and how far south the\nfront moves. Some models keep the front north of the area while\nothers bring the front through the area. If the front remains \nnorth, highs in the 90s could continue into the middle of next \nweek, if the front moves further south highs in the 80s and some\nshower and thunderstorm chances will occur.",
